-- title:
--   Base-point freeness of the embedding system on X₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and write $F_N$ for `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the coefficientwise image of the full modular function field of level $N$ (the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the divisor expansions of level $N$). Let $r$ be a natural number and $s : \mathrm{Fin}\,r \to F_N$ a family satisfying `IsEmbBasis N s`, that is: $s$ is linearly independent over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-span of its range is exactly the Riemann–Roch space $\{f : \forall v,\ v(f) \le \exp(D(v))\}$ of the divisor $D =$ `embDivisor N` $= (2\,\mathrm{genusFF}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}, F_N) + 1)\cdot \overline{\infty}$, supported at the cusp place `cuspInftyBar N`. Let $w$ be any place of $F_N$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, i.e. a proper valuation subring containing the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and a principal ideal ring. Then there is an index $i$ with $\mathrm{ord}_w(s\,i) + D(w) = 0$, where $\mathrm{ord}_w$ is minus the logarithm of the associated adic valuation: some member of the family attains the bound imposed by $D$ exactly at $w$.
--
--   This is the base-point freeness of the complete linear system attached to the divisor $(2g+1)\overline{\infty}$ on the modular curve of level $N$, stated for an arbitrary basis of its Riemann–Roch space. It is used in the construction of the height form attached to $J_0(N)$, in particular in the estimates for hyperplane sections and in comparisons of the archimedean embedding away from the support.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_ord_add_embDivisor_eq_zero.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_JZeroHeightForm

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
